      "fix_text": "Note: The following instructions use the PGDATA and PGVER environment variables. Refer to APPENDIX-F for instructions on configuring PGDATA and APPENDIX-H for PGVER. To ensure logging is enabled, review supplementary content APPENDIX-C for instructions on enabling logging.\n\nIf logging is enabled, the following configurations must be made to log unsuccessful connections, date/time, username, and session identifier.\n\nAs the database administrator (shown here as \"postgres\"), edit postgresql.conf: \n\n$ sudo su - postgres \n$ vi ${PGDATA?}/postgresql.conf \n\nEdit the following parameters: \n\nlog_connections = on \nlog_line_prefix = '< %m %u %c: >' \npgaudit.log = 'read, write' \n\nWhere: \n* %m is the time and date \n* %u is the username \n* %c is the session ID for the connection \n\nAs the system administrator, reload the server with the new configuration: \n\n$ sudo systemctl reload postgresql-${PGVER?}"
